# HTTP contract

- An approved feature specification is the source of truth for the endpoint or
  client change being implemented.
- `docs/api.md` is the consolidated source of truth for published endpoints,
  payloads, responses, errors, and authentication.
- `openapi.yaml` at the repository root and backend Swagger UI at `/api/docs`
  must stay aligned with that contract.
- Read both the specification and `docs/api.md` before adding or changing an
  endpoint or API client.
- Do not invent product routes, fields, statuses, integrations, or side
  effects beyond the approved specification. Technical HTTP shape is decided
  in the specification by a senior agent. Ask the human when an HTTP change
  would add a public route or change authentication or authorization policy.
- Update `docs/api.md`, `openapi.yaml`, and Swagger in the same change when an
  approved feature changes the HTTP contract.
